WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.085
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.623 --> 00:07.975
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.010 --> 00:11.648
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.660 --> 00:14.479
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.513 --> 00:17.583
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.634 --> 00:21.487
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.521 --> 00:23.122
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.156 --> 00:25.024
♪ Laugh and cry

00:25.058 --> 00:27.828
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.805 --> 00:37.439
Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.

00:37.473 --> 00:40.244
This just in: Wanted fugitive,
Bobby "The Shirt" Briggs,

00:40.278 --> 00:42.580
notorious for always wearing
shirts while committing

00:42.614 --> 00:44.349
his crimes,
has finally been caught

00:44.383 --> 00:46.150
after 15 years on the lam.

00:46.184 --> 00:48.153
A police spokesperson
was quoted as saying,

00:48.187 --> 00:49.537
"Duh, I'm a dumb cop.

00:49.572 --> 00:51.440
I like to give
Tom Tucker a ticket."

00:51.475 --> 00:53.110
I was going, like, 41.

00:53.144 --> 00:55.111
Oh, my God,
I don't believe it.

00:55.145 --> 00:57.381
They finally got that
son of a bitch, Briggs.

00:57.415 --> 00:58.381
You know that guy?

00:58.415 --> 01:00.150
You're damn right, I do.

01:00.184 --> 01:03.054
Bobby Briggs is the one who
put me in this wheelchair.

01:03.088 --> 01:04.656
(crying):
They got him.

01:04.690 --> 01:06.124
They finally got him.

01:06.158 --> 01:07.760
Geez, Joe, you okay?

01:07.794 --> 01:10.496
(crying)

01:10.530 --> 01:12.432
Here, use my handkerchief.

01:12.466 --> 01:13.718
It's wet and cold.

01:13.752 --> 01:15.318
Well, yeah,
it's my handkerchief.

01:15.353 --> 01:17.121
I've been blowing
my nose in it all day.

01:17.123 --> 01:19.323
Wait a minute, Bobby Briggs
is the one who crippled you?

01:19.358 --> 01:21.026
You always told us
you fell off a roof

01:21.060 --> 01:22.195
during a fight with the Grinch.

01:22.229 --> 01:24.397
(sighs) I lied.

01:24.431 --> 01:27.634
I lied because I was ashamed
of the real story:

01:27.668 --> 01:30.105
that I let a vicious
criminal get away.

01:30.139 --> 01:31.170
What happened?

01:31.205 --> 01:32.640
Well, it was 1996.

01:32.674 --> 01:34.559
Briggs was one of the
biggest heroin dealers

01:34.593 --> 01:37.095
east of Providence, which is
mostly just open water,

01:37.129 --> 01:40.181
but still, I'd been undercover,
tracking his operation

01:40.232 --> 01:43.653
for six months and had finally
gained his confidence.

01:48.276 --> 01:50.244
<i>I had almost
gathered enough evidence</i>

01:50.279 --> 01:51.880
<i>to put Briggsaway for good,</i>

01:51.915 --> 01:53.232
<i>but I knew a taped confession</i>

01:53.266 --> 01:54.667
<i>would make the case
a slam dunk.</i>

01:54.701 --> 01:56.702
This is gonna take us
to the next level.

01:56.736 --> 01:58.672
We're gonna be banging
so many hot chicks

01:58.706 --> 02:00.373
with jeans up to
their navels.

02:00.408 --> 02:02.543
Bobby Briggs, you're
really good at heroin.

02:02.577 --> 02:04.779
How much heroin
is here, Bobby Briggs?

02:04.813 --> 02:06.214
Why are you
talking like that?

02:06.249 --> 02:08.050
Are you wearing a wire?

02:09.267 --> 02:11.720
Oh, you're dead,
Joe Swansonson.

02:11.754 --> 02:13.923
<i>My undercover name
was Swansonson.</i>

02:13.957 --> 02:15.258
Easy, Briggs.

02:15.292 --> 02:17.660
You kill a cop,
they'll put you away forever.

02:17.695 --> 02:20.432
Then get ready to spend
the rest of your life

02:20.466 --> 02:22.967
as a lame gimp
with an annoying-voiced wife.

02:23.002 --> 02:24.135
<i>He'd met Bonnie.</i>

02:24.170 --> 02:27.073
(screaming in pain)

02:28.810 --> 02:30.459
<i>Briggs got away,</i>

02:30.494 --> 02:32.212
and I've been in this wheelchair
ever since.

02:32.246 --> 02:34.164
I like that you
can tell me a story

02:34.198 --> 02:36.267
starting at the Clam
and ending on a Ferris wheel.

02:36.301 --> 02:37.569
Yeah, people
are starving in Africa,

02:37.604 --> 02:38.954
and I'm at a carnival

02:38.988 --> 02:41.341
with my best buddies
on a beautiful night.

02:41.375 --> 02:44.093
Blessings. Blessings.

02:48.315 --> 02:50.800
So, Joe, it must
feel great to finally

02:50.835 --> 02:52.536
have some closure
with Bobby Briggs.

02:52.571 --> 02:53.839
Yeah.

02:53.873 --> 02:56.108
You know last night was
the first time in 15 years

02:56.142 --> 02:57.659
I didn't strangle
Bonnie in my sleep?

02:57.694 --> 02:59.327
Okay.

02:59.362 --> 03:02.299
Hey, Dad, you're gonna
want to see this.

03:03.901 --> 03:05.686
Again recapping
our breaking news,

03:05.720 --> 03:09.140
longtime fugitive Bobby Briggs
has escaped from police custody.

03:09.175 --> 03:11.276
His whereabouts
are currently unknown.

03:11.310 --> 03:13.696
News of Briggs's escape
first broke on Telemundo,

03:13.730 --> 03:15.165
if you can believe that.

03:15.199 --> 03:17.517
<i>Escapo!
Escapo! Escapo!</i>

03:17.552 --> 03:20.069
Briggs reportedly escaped
during a prison open house,

03:20.103 --> 03:22.840
an event that will most likely
be canceled in the future.

03:22.875 --> 03:25.476
No, no!
I can't believe it.

03:25.511 --> 03:27.146
Oh, don't worry, Joe,
they'll get him back.

03:27.180 --> 03:28.346
No, they won't!

03:28.380 --> 03:30.749
It took 15 years
to catch him.

03:30.784 --> 03:33.051
Well, this seems like a good
time to be heading out.

03:33.086 --> 03:34.370
I should be getting back anyway.

03:34.405 --> 03:35.940
I left Rupert with a sitter.

03:35.974 --> 03:37.374
Well, you know
where everything is.

03:37.409 --> 03:39.578
Feel free to help yourself
to anything in the fridge.

03:39.612 --> 03:44.450
And Mr. Con Man here can have
pudding or ice cream, not both.

03:48.089 --> 03:49.907
Chief, can I have a word?

03:49.941 --> 03:51.875
Yeah, but first,
you have to agree

03:51.911 --> 03:53.377
there's a huge
difference

03:53.411 --> 03:55.546
between bisexual men
and homosexual men.

03:55.580 --> 03:57.147
Sure, Chief.
Thank you. Huge.

03:57.182 --> 03:58.883
What is it?

03:58.918 --> 04:00.419
Well, Chief, I'm here
because I want you

04:00.453 --> 04:01.786
to put me on the Briggs case.

04:01.821 --> 04:02.922
Absolutely not.

04:02.956 --> 04:03.756
Come on, Chief!

04:03.790 --> 04:05.025
I know everything about Briggs.

04:05.059 --> 04:07.060
I'm the only one
who can catch him.

04:07.094 --> 04:09.197
No, Swanson, you're
too close to the case.

04:09.231 --> 04:11.032
I'm putting Officers
Grant and Casey on it

04:11.066 --> 04:12.768
because they're so
far from the case,

04:12.802 --> 04:14.268
they don't care
about it at all.

04:14.303 --> 04:16.104
Hi, Chief.
Hi.

04:16.139 --> 04:17.273
This isn't fair!

04:17.308 --> 04:18.941
Swanson, you know
your assignment.

04:18.975 --> 04:20.643
You get me the guy who's
been rubbing his butt

04:20.678 --> 04:22.312
all over Dunkin' Donuts.

04:23.348 --> 04:24.582
Can I help you?

04:24.616 --> 04:26.017
Not illegal. Not illegal.

04:26.052 --> 04:27.752
Show me the law.
Not illegal.

04:31.791 --> 04:33.793
Hey, Joe, look,
I know you're down

04:33.827 --> 04:36.162
about this Briggs thing,
and that kind of bums me out,

04:36.196 --> 04:37.814
so I got you
this Cookie Puss.

04:37.849 --> 04:39.165
(laughs)
Isn't that funny?

04:39.199 --> 04:40.968
Look at that weird nose.

04:41.002 --> 04:43.337
I think your nose
is weird.

04:43.371 --> 04:45.073
Guys, I'm telling you, I...

04:45.107 --> 04:47.342
I just don't think
I could live with Briggs

04:47.376 --> 04:49.411
on the lam for another 15 years.

04:49.446 --> 04:51.214
Well, why don't you
do something about it?

04:51.249 --> 04:53.483
I can't do anything about it.
The chief won't let me.

04:53.517 --> 04:54.819
Joe, if they don't
find this guy,

04:54.853 --> 04:57.021
it's gonna eat you alive
for the rest of your life.

04:57.055 --> 04:58.657
You got to take matters
into your own hands.

04:58.691 --> 04:59.991
You got to go after this guy.

05:00.025 --> 05:01.860
But that's a breach
of police protocol.

05:01.895 --> 05:03.563
This isn't about you
as a cop.

05:03.597 --> 05:05.064
This is
about you as a man.

05:05.099 --> 05:06.765
Come on, what do you say?

05:06.799 --> 05:09.051
Quagmire and I will help you
bring this guy to justice.

05:09.086 --> 05:10.320
(chuckles) Peter,
what did I say

05:10.354 --> 05:12.388
about you volunteering
me for (bleep)?

05:12.423 --> 05:14.525
All right, let's do it!

05:14.559 --> 05:16.211
MAYOR WEST:
Well, if you're gonna do it,

05:16.245 --> 05:18.980
you're gonna need someone
who's very good at disguise.

05:19.015 --> 05:20.549
Who said that?

05:20.583 --> 05:22.551
I'd love to go with you,
but I can't.

05:22.586 --> 05:24.187
I'm supposed to be
the gift table

05:24.222 --> 05:26.156
at a Bar Mitzvah tomorrow.

05:32.049 --> 05:34.016
All right, if we're
gonna go after Briggs,

05:34.050 --> 05:35.952
this might be a good
place to start.

05:38.323 --> 05:40.191
I've spent the
last 15 years

05:40.225 --> 05:41.708
gathering
information on him,

05:41.742 --> 05:43.344
and it's all here.

05:43.378 --> 05:45.230
Every crime he's committed,
every associate he's...

05:45.248 --> 05:47.799
Oh, look, Briggs
was All-County JV swimming.

05:47.834 --> 05:49.635
Well, I don't just
focus on the negative.

05:49.670 --> 05:53.006
Joe, your 25-year-old son
and your baby daughter share

05:53.041 --> 05:55.542
<i>a room just so you can keep
a weirdo Beautiful Mind room?</i>

05:55.577 --> 05:57.178
Isn't that a little bizarre?

05:57.213 --> 06:00.915
And then we dug the bullets out
of that Iraqi family's skulls

06:00.950 --> 06:02.750
so they couldn't
be traced back to us.

06:02.785 --> 06:05.387
<i>MAN'S VOICE:
Today, I saw a balloon.</i>

06:05.423 --> 06:07.824
Briggs' FBI profile
says the only relationship

06:07.859 --> 06:11.628
he's maintained over the years
is with a stripper named Tanya.

06:11.662 --> 06:13.131
Tax records show
she currently works

06:13.165 --> 06:14.733
at a club in Atlantic City.

06:14.767 --> 06:15.968
So that's our first stop.

06:16.002 --> 06:17.568
Is there touching
at the club?

06:17.603 --> 06:19.971
I-I-I don't know,
Peter. Maybe.

06:20.005 --> 06:21.640
Okay, this is good,
this is good.

06:21.674 --> 06:23.709
I'll be sure to pack
my blamming jeans.

06:26.982 --> 06:28.314
Hey, listen,
thanks for agreeing

06:28.349 --> 06:30.619
to take care of Principessa
while we're gone, Lois.

06:30.653 --> 06:31.652
It's our pleasure.

06:31.686 --> 06:33.121
She looks like
a nice kitty.

06:33.156 --> 06:34.657
Uh, kitty?

06:34.691 --> 06:36.324
Lois, she is
a purebred Persian.

06:36.359 --> 06:39.396
I can trace her lineage
to the cats kept by Cleopatra.

06:39.430 --> 06:41.265
Just tell me what
I need to do, Glenn.

06:41.299 --> 06:43.101
Well, first, she has
a very active bowel.

06:43.135 --> 06:45.002
You can't be too generous
with the baby wipes.

06:45.036 --> 06:47.323
Stroke front to back
like you would on yourself.

06:47.357 --> 06:49.642
Otherwise, you're smashing
feces into her genitals.

06:49.676 --> 06:50.893
Also, she's very skittish,

06:50.927 --> 06:52.861
so you have to
touch her like this.

06:52.895 --> 06:55.599
I'm going to touch you now.

06:55.633 --> 06:56.799
Is that okay?

06:56.833 --> 06:58.618
See how I'm going?

06:58.653 --> 07:03.558
Slowly, slowly.

07:03.592 --> 07:06.528
Oh, the mysteries
you keep inside of you.

07:06.563 --> 07:08.915
PETER: Quagmire, come on,
let's go.

07:09.999 --> 07:11.851
All right, I guess we're off.

07:11.886 --> 07:13.153
Hey, you guys,
check out the look

07:13.188 --> 07:14.788
on Lois's face
when I do this.

07:14.823 --> 07:16.725
(tires screech)

07:16.759 --> 07:17.925
Peter!

07:17.959 --> 07:20.028
Clean that up, you idiot!

07:20.062 --> 07:21.247
Love you.

07:27.855 --> 07:31.074
Boy, it'll be satisfying
to finally slap the cuffs

07:31.125 --> 07:32.859
on Briggs once and for all.

07:32.877 --> 07:34.861
Hey, you ever just drive
through a town and wonder,

07:34.879 --> 07:36.998
"Who the hell lives here?"
All the time.

07:37.032 --> 07:39.200
Look at this place.
I mean, what-what's going on?

07:39.218 --> 07:41.253
There's an adult
with a lemonade stand.

07:41.304 --> 07:42.922
That Chinese restaurant
still has the sign

07:42.973 --> 07:44.207
from when it was a mechanic.

07:44.225 --> 07:45.676
I don't want to eat lo mein

07:45.710 --> 07:47.260
where they were
just changing mufflers.

07:47.311 --> 07:49.765
There's an apartment
above that Arby's.

07:49.816 --> 07:51.548
With toys in the window.

07:51.567 --> 07:53.051
Someone has built
a life up there.

07:53.069 --> 07:54.470
What a mess.

07:54.505 --> 07:56.155
I'm telling you,
the Founding Fathers would be

07:56.190 --> 07:58.058
very disappointed in
where their country ended up.

07:58.076 --> 08:00.227
Eh, it wasn't so perfect
back then, either.

08:00.245 --> 08:02.029
And so I say unto you,

08:02.063 --> 08:04.765
sons of liberty,
no longer will free men

08:04.799 --> 08:08.035
live under the yoke
of giant predatory birds.

08:08.069 --> 08:11.607
Shrieking, swooping down,
stealing our livestock.

08:11.641 --> 08:13.042
What's going on in here?

08:13.076 --> 08:15.779
N-Nothing, uh, just
bellyaching about the British.

08:15.812 --> 08:17.614
Get back to warming
those eggs.

08:20.084 --> 08:22.036
(muffled music playing)

08:22.071 --> 08:23.505
(brakes screech)

08:23.540 --> 08:25.557
♪

08:27.845 --> 08:29.529
All right,
this is the place.

08:29.563 --> 08:32.033
We got to see if we
can find Briggs's girl.

08:32.067 --> 08:33.768
Hey, we're looking
for a stripper named Tanya.

08:33.802 --> 08:35.069
She here tonight?

08:35.103 --> 08:36.904
Yeah, she's working
the Champagne Room.

08:36.938 --> 08:38.573
Follow me.

08:40.243 --> 08:41.709
Hey, Quagmire, you, uh...

08:41.743 --> 08:43.578
you ever been to
Atlantic City before?

08:43.612 --> 08:45.797
Once, about 20
years ago. Why?

08:45.832 --> 08:47.550
All right!
All right!

08:47.584 --> 08:49.252
All right!
All right!

08:49.286 --> 08:51.839
Hey, are you Tanya?

08:51.873 --> 08:53.407
Yeah. Who are you?

08:53.441 --> 08:54.976
A guy who's looking
for Bobby Briggs.

08:55.011 --> 08:56.177
Where is he?

08:56.212 --> 08:57.712
I don't know any Bobby Briggs.

08:57.747 --> 08:59.615
And even if I did,
I wouldn't tell you.

08:59.650 --> 09:00.633
You're lying!

09:00.652 --> 09:01.934
Joe, let me handle this.

09:01.968 --> 09:03.620
I know how to communicate
with strippers.

09:03.655 --> 09:05.056
All I need is one dance,

09:05.090 --> 09:06.991
and I'll know
everything she knows.

09:07.026 --> 09:08.309
You free for a dance?

09:08.344 --> 09:10.194
Sure.

09:11.614 --> 09:12.581
I need information.

09:12.615 --> 09:14.199
I was molested by my dad.

09:14.250 --> 09:16.201
I know that.
I need other information.

09:16.252 --> 09:18.671
I want you to tell me
where I can find Bobby Briggs.

09:18.705 --> 09:20.623
Come on, you know
I can't give out

09:20.658 --> 09:22.293
a client's personal
information.

09:22.327 --> 09:25.697
All right, I'm gonna have
to do the Vulcan V-Meld.

09:25.732 --> 09:27.732
♪

09:36.778 --> 09:38.680
He lives at 2820
Ocean Boulevard,

09:38.714 --> 09:40.682
across from the park,
apartment two.

09:40.716 --> 09:41.649
Atta girl.

09:41.684 --> 09:43.985
Okay, now spit
in your own mouth.

09:44.019 --> 09:45.938
This is a cool place.

09:49.043 --> 09:52.044
Boy, it sure is nice having
Mr. Quagmire's cat around.

09:52.079 --> 09:54.748
I got to say, cats are
so much better than dogs.

09:54.782 --> 09:56.768
Well, that's kind of
a broad statement.

09:56.793 --> 09:57.719
It's true.

09:57.720 --> 10:00.221
Okay, show me one way in which
cats are better than dogs.

10:00.255 --> 10:02.191
Well, okay, uh,
for one thing,

10:02.225 --> 10:03.727
they always land
on their feet.

10:03.761 --> 10:05.260
Watch.

10:05.312 --> 10:07.147
So? Big deal.
Dogs do that, too.

10:07.181 --> 10:09.734
Here, go ahead, do what you
just did, but with me.

10:09.768 --> 10:11.686
Ow! Oh, my God!

10:11.720 --> 10:13.270
Oh, my neck! Ow!

10:13.305 --> 10:15.107
Oh, my God, Brian!

10:15.141 --> 10:17.175
Don't touch me! Don't touch me!
Call somebody! Oh!

10:17.210 --> 10:18.611
We need one of
those boards

10:18.645 --> 10:20.647
they use for
football players! Ow!

10:20.682 --> 10:22.199
Hey, what's going on?

10:22.233 --> 10:23.367
Nothing.

10:23.401 --> 10:26.955
I just figured out
why cats are better than babies.

10:26.989 --> 10:28.957
Well, that's kind of
a broad statement.

10:31.343 --> 10:34.647
Okay, 2820 Ocean,
this is it.

10:40.254 --> 10:42.389
All right, apartment number two.

10:42.423 --> 10:43.758
We'll just pick the lock.

10:48.314 --> 10:50.083
What? What is that?

10:50.117 --> 10:53.771
Let's use our eyes to see.

10:57.718 --> 10:59.685
Aw, this guy has sugar cereals.

10:59.720 --> 11:01.254
His mom must be so cool.

11:01.288 --> 11:02.839
And he's got a trash compactor.

11:04.324 --> 11:05.625
(machine clattering)

11:05.659 --> 11:07.093
It compacted it all.

11:07.127 --> 11:09.163
That is so boss.

11:14.654 --> 11:17.122
Aha! We meet again, Briggs.

11:17.157 --> 11:18.491
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Who are you?

11:18.526 --> 11:19.959
Joe Swanson.

11:19.993 --> 11:21.261
Who?

11:21.295 --> 11:23.947
Wait, you... you
don't remember me?

11:23.981 --> 11:26.217
I infiltrated your
heroin operation.

11:26.251 --> 11:27.985
<i>We saw Reality Bites
together.</i>

11:28.020 --> 11:29.988
(Joe groans)

11:30.023 --> 11:32.124
You guys, I found him!

11:32.158 --> 11:33.977
He went that way!

11:39.701 --> 11:41.435
(grunts)

11:49.545 --> 11:51.530
(cell phone ringing)

11:51.565 --> 11:52.832
Damn it. That's Lois.

11:52.866 --> 11:54.801
If I don't get this,
she's going to kill me.

11:54.836 --> 11:56.638
(grunting)

11:59.408 --> 12:01.192
Hi, sweetie.

12:01.227 --> 12:03.329
Yeah, everything's great.

12:03.363 --> 12:05.598
Of course, I miss you.

12:05.632 --> 12:08.368
Well, how does the supermarket
run out of parsley?

12:08.403 --> 12:09.803
I'm as angry as you are.

12:09.837 --> 12:11.522
Peter, I'm going to fall!

12:20.416 --> 12:22.150
It looks like
you're out of roof.

12:31.196 --> 12:33.164
Damn it.
There's no way across.

12:33.199 --> 12:35.300
Spidey, can you swing us
across with your web?

12:35.334 --> 12:37.270
No, I can't
swing you across.

12:37.304 --> 12:39.071
And it's Spider-Man,
not Spidey.

12:39.106 --> 12:40.974
I'm pretty sure I've heard
people call you Spidey.

12:41.009 --> 12:42.443
Yeah, close friends.

12:42.478 --> 12:43.677
What's your name?
Peter.

12:43.711 --> 12:45.380
Hey, Petey,
do stuff for me.

12:45.414 --> 12:47.448
Oh, I don't like that.
Yeah, you don't like it.

12:47.483 --> 12:49.551
And you're a fat nobody,
and I'm (bleep) Spider-Man,

12:49.586 --> 12:51.419
so how do you
think I feel?

12:54.642 --> 12:56.693
He's getting away.
Guys, drop me over the side!

12:56.727 --> 12:57.861
Are you crazy, Joe?!

12:57.895 --> 12:59.213
That fall
will kill you.

12:59.247 --> 13:01.248
Not if I land on my legs.

13:03.802 --> 13:05.003
(grunting)

13:05.054 --> 13:06.839
PETER:
Heads up.

13:08.157 --> 13:10.226
(panting)

13:11.479 --> 13:13.063
I got you now, Briggs.

13:25.880 --> 13:29.215
CROWD:
Move that bus!

13:29.249 --> 13:31.618
(cheering)

13:31.652 --> 13:33.103
(gasps)

13:33.137 --> 13:35.773
Enjoy your new home.

13:37.159 --> 13:38.711
He's gone, you guys!

13:38.745 --> 13:39.878
I had him!

13:39.929 --> 13:41.447
That was our one chance!

13:41.481 --> 13:42.582
It's all right, Joe.

13:42.616 --> 13:44.017
You got nothing
to be ashamed of.

13:44.051 --> 13:45.052
You're a great cop

13:45.087 --> 13:46.353
with a very
distinguished career.

13:46.387 --> 13:47.888
You caught that guy
who was killing

13:47.923 --> 13:49.057
all those
Filipino girls.

13:49.092 --> 13:50.826
Yeah, but this was important!

13:50.860 --> 13:52.627
This was the guy
who ruined my life.

13:52.662 --> 13:54.931
The one perp
who meant everything to me.

13:54.965 --> 13:56.282
If I caught this guy,

13:56.316 --> 13:58.017
I'd finally be able
to sleep at night.

13:58.052 --> 13:59.136
Damn it!

13:59.170 --> 14:00.204
(siren whoops)

14:00.238 --> 14:01.623
Oh, thank God. Cops.

14:01.657 --> 14:02.655
Oh, good.

14:02.689 --> 14:03.891
You guys
can still catch Briggs.

14:03.925 --> 14:04.992
He's headed that way.

14:05.026 --> 14:06.194
We're not here for him.

14:06.212 --> 14:07.328
We're here for you guys.

14:07.362 --> 14:08.797
You're under arrest
for interfering

14:08.831 --> 14:10.366
with a police
investigation.

14:10.400 --> 14:11.534
What?

14:11.568 --> 14:12.835
Yeah, what the hell?

14:12.869 --> 14:15.004
You should be out there
arresting the real criminals.

14:15.038 --> 14:16.306
Like switchblade-wielding
white guys

14:16.340 --> 14:19.109
from movies and TV
who don't talk like people talk.

14:19.143 --> 14:20.445
Easy, mama.

14:20.479 --> 14:21.897
Hand over that purse,
and everything

14:21.931 --> 14:23.948
will be real cool,
you dig?

14:29.078 --> 14:30.913
Guys, you got to let us
out of here.

14:30.947 --> 14:32.113
The real criminal's
getting away.

14:32.148 --> 14:33.783
Yeah, the bastard's
making a break for it,

14:33.817 --> 14:35.568
just like
South America.

14:35.602 --> 14:36.887
Hmm.

14:36.921 --> 14:39.322
Lot of black guys over there.

14:39.374 --> 14:40.874
Hey, man,
where you going?

14:40.908 --> 14:42.275
I'll be back.
I'm coming back.

14:42.293 --> 14:43.561
I'll be right back.

14:43.595 --> 14:45.129
Why would the cops
arrest us

14:45.164 --> 14:47.266
instead of going
after Briggs?

14:49.903 --> 14:51.404
Flannigan?
Wait a minute.

14:51.439 --> 14:53.606
That's one of the corrupt cops
who helped harbor Briggs

14:53.641 --> 14:55.609
while he was on the lam
for 15 years.

14:55.644 --> 14:56.976
These guys are bad news.

14:57.011 --> 14:58.145
Oh, my God.

14:58.180 --> 14:59.798
What are they
going to do to us?

14:59.816 --> 15:01.650
We're not going to stick around
to find out.

15:01.684 --> 15:03.452
Joe, hold your handcuffs
over my lap.

15:03.486 --> 15:04.587
(zip)

15:04.621 --> 15:05.755
What the hell is that?

15:05.789 --> 15:07.090
Swiss Army penis.

15:07.124 --> 15:08.509
(sawing)

15:08.543 --> 15:10.277
Wow, Quagmire.
That's incredible.

15:10.311 --> 15:11.578
Peter?

15:11.613 --> 15:12.680
(sawing)

15:12.715 --> 15:14.348
Yours are made
of a stronger metal.

15:14.382 --> 15:17.451
We're going to have to go
with the acetylene torch penis.

15:17.485 --> 15:18.953
Don't...
don't look right at it.

15:18.987 --> 15:21.940
My STDs help it
burn brighter.

15:23.326 --> 15:25.128
The keys are in
the ignition. Let's go!

15:27.014 --> 15:29.550
I told you to search
that guy's penis.

15:29.585 --> 15:31.636
You say that
about everybody.

15:33.156 --> 15:34.839
Yeah, we did it!
But we lost Briggs.

15:34.857 --> 15:36.475
How are we
going to find him now?

15:36.509 --> 15:37.727
We got nothing.

15:37.778 --> 15:39.729
Well, I don't know if
it helps, but I found

15:39.780 --> 15:41.532
this number next to the
phone in his kitchen.

15:41.566 --> 15:43.617
I was saving it 'cause
I was going to make

15:43.652 --> 15:45.202
a scrapbook of the
trip for you guys.

15:45.237 --> 15:46.454
Let me see that.

15:46.488 --> 15:48.690
This is the area code
for Juarez, Mexico.

15:48.708 --> 15:50.358
He's trying to get
over the border!

15:50.376 --> 15:52.327
You think so?
Definitely.

15:52.361 --> 15:53.830
There's only one road
into Juarez,

15:53.864 --> 15:55.413
and it goes
through El Paso.

15:55.465 --> 15:57.083
We got to get
to El Paso.

15:57.134 --> 15:58.418
Joe, how do you know

15:58.470 --> 15:59.970
the area code for
Juarez, Mexico?

16:00.004 --> 16:02.924
There was a stem cell doctor
I went down there to see.

16:02.975 --> 16:05.960
He just rubbed, like,
salsa on my legs.

16:09.199 --> 16:11.034
Hey, you're not
in uniform.

16:11.068 --> 16:12.803
Are you guys cops?

16:12.837 --> 16:14.504
Are you guys cops?

16:14.540 --> 16:16.022
They know we're not cops!

16:16.057 --> 16:17.057
(tires squealing)

16:22.582 --> 16:24.049
All right, guys,
the next flight

16:24.083 --> 16:25.517
to El Paso leaves
in 40 minutes.

16:25.552 --> 16:26.819
But Briggs is ahead of us.

16:26.853 --> 16:28.120
Won't he already be there?

16:28.154 --> 16:30.156
No, he'd never risk
going through an airport.

16:30.191 --> 16:31.575
Too many cops,
too many cameras,

16:31.610 --> 16:32.609
too much security.

16:32.643 --> 16:33.811
I don't know, Joe.

16:33.845 --> 16:35.547
Sometimes the
security's pretty lax.

16:35.581 --> 16:37.749
I mean, the last plane
I was on got gay-jacked.

16:37.767 --> 16:40.453
This plane's going to Miami!

16:40.487 --> 16:42.087
(passengers gasp)

16:42.105 --> 16:44.107
(electronic dance music playing)

16:52.402 --> 16:53.501
Hey, Lois?

16:53.536 --> 16:54.970
Shh. Quiet, Brian.

16:55.005 --> 16:56.740
Mom's taking a nap
on the couch.

16:56.774 --> 16:58.608
Yeah. And look,
she fell asleep

16:58.626 --> 17:00.861
with the cat right
on her chest.

17:09.389 --> 17:11.273
Isn't that cute?

17:12.642 --> 17:14.643
(purring)

17:23.906 --> 17:25.273
Meow.

17:25.308 --> 17:27.342
Purr. Purr.

17:27.376 --> 17:29.345
I think you're dreaming.

17:29.379 --> 17:31.497
No, I'm not.

17:37.171 --> 17:38.940
BRIAN:
Stupid cat!

17:42.612 --> 17:44.246
God, it's so damn hot.

17:44.281 --> 17:45.547
Hey, I got an idea.

17:45.582 --> 17:47.933
Let's make
scalding asphalt angels.

17:47.968 --> 17:50.387
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

17:50.438 --> 17:51.605
(sizzling)

17:51.639 --> 17:54.575
Second-degree burns;
first-degree fun.

17:54.610 --> 17:56.845
Geez, how long we got to
stand out here like this?

17:56.879 --> 17:57.980
Till Briggs comes through.

17:58.014 --> 17:59.682
You know, I was thinking
about that, Joe.

17:59.717 --> 18:02.151
If Briggs is driving here,
that's like 2,000 miles.

18:02.186 --> 18:04.287
It's going to be at
least a couple of days.

18:04.321 --> 18:06.073
Huh. I guess you're right.

18:06.107 --> 18:08.592
Well, what are we going to do
for two days in El Paso?

18:09.962 --> 18:11.831
There's a Chicano
heritage festival.

18:11.865 --> 18:13.097
No way.

18:13.131 --> 18:14.766
KC and the Sunshine Band
is playing.

18:14.800 --> 18:15.935
Why?

18:15.969 --> 18:17.402
Or we could visit
the Pershing House

18:17.436 --> 18:19.105
where John Pershing
took control

18:19.139 --> 18:21.440
of the Eighth Army
Brigade in 1914.

18:22.644 --> 18:23.911
So, that's his bed?
Yes.

18:23.946 --> 18:25.345
So, that's his desk?
Yes.

18:25.380 --> 18:26.748
So, that's his lamp?
Yes.

18:26.782 --> 18:28.150
So, that's his dresser?
Yes.

18:28.184 --> 18:29.651
So, that's his window?
Yes.

18:29.685 --> 18:30.986
So, that's his floor?
Yes.

18:31.021 --> 18:32.689
Wow.

18:36.895 --> 18:38.228
What do you got
there, Quagmire?

18:38.262 --> 18:39.463
Is that Briggs?

18:39.498 --> 18:40.732
No, this guy's clean.

18:40.767 --> 18:42.466
Well, send him through.
What's the holdup?

18:42.501 --> 18:43.902
Sombreros! Maracas!

18:43.936 --> 18:45.837
Ceramic Winnie the Pooh dolls!

18:45.872 --> 18:47.073
Get 'em now, folks!

18:47.107 --> 18:49.342
You're not going to find
this stuff in Mexico!

18:50.443 --> 18:52.662
Come on. What's
going on up there?

18:52.696 --> 18:54.530
Briggs.

18:57.937 --> 19:00.088
Damn it!
He's getting away!

19:22.083 --> 19:23.949
(grunts)

19:26.905 --> 19:29.673
You're not going to get away
this time, you son of a bitch.

19:29.708 --> 19:31.009
Please, don't kill me.

19:31.044 --> 19:32.209
I'm not married.

19:32.244 --> 19:33.678
My life is awesome.

19:33.730 --> 19:36.732
I've waited 15 years
for this moment, Briggs.

19:36.766 --> 19:38.735
Do you have any idea
what it's like

19:38.769 --> 19:41.638
to have to lift yourself
into a wheelchair every morning?

19:41.656 --> 19:44.324
To have your wife look at you
like you're half a man?

19:44.359 --> 19:45.977
To get preferential parking?

19:46.011 --> 19:48.164
To board a plane early
with the first-class people

19:48.198 --> 19:49.665
and gold card members?

19:49.699 --> 19:51.417
All right, it's not all bad.

19:51.451 --> 19:53.252
But I'm not going to kill you.

19:53.286 --> 19:55.790
I'm not an animal like you.

19:55.824 --> 19:57.557
So, what are you going to do,
arrest me?

19:57.592 --> 19:58.726
No.

19:58.761 --> 20:00.661
I don't arrest cripples.

20:00.679 --> 20:03.297
(groaning)

20:03.331 --> 20:05.017
By the way, you're under arrest.

20:05.050 --> 20:07.553
I only said that last thing
'cause it seemed cool.

20:07.604 --> 20:09.288
Oh, my God,
that was so awesome.

20:09.322 --> 20:10.590
I saw everything.

20:10.624 --> 20:11.991
You were all like...
(deep mumbling)

20:12.026 --> 20:13.726
And Briggs was all like...
(high-pitched mumbling)

20:13.761 --> 20:15.629
And then you were all like...
(mimics two gunshots)

20:15.664 --> 20:17.265
And then Briggs's legs
were like...

20:17.300 --> 20:18.900
(mimics video game
sound effects)

20:18.935 --> 20:20.318
Oh, crap, he's dead.

20:20.352 --> 20:21.654
I think he bled out.

20:21.688 --> 20:23.489
I must have hit
the femoral artery.

20:23.523 --> 20:25.709
Ah, just kick him into Mexico.

20:29.999 --> 20:32.467
Guys, I can't thank you
enough for what you did.

20:32.501 --> 20:34.170
You risked your
lives for me,

20:34.204 --> 20:35.837
and I couldn't have
done it without you.

20:35.871 --> 20:37.490
Hey, that's what
pals are for.

20:37.524 --> 20:38.756
Yeah, and thanks for letting me

20:38.791 --> 20:40.543
fire a few rounds
into Briggs's corpse.

20:40.577 --> 20:43.546
That was the most powerful
I've felt in a couple years.

20:43.580 --> 20:44.681
Well, you guys helped me

20:44.715 --> 20:46.468
finally have some closure
in my life.

20:46.550 --> 20:49.038
I feel like a new man--
like I'm reborn.

20:49.421 --> 20:52.781
Joe, you have blood just
pouring out of your pant leg.

20:53.000 --> 20:55.368
Yeah, I had a ball
blow in the river.

20:55.369 --> 21:56.369
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru